# Set the live tool-tip frame offset used by the servo controller.
#
# The offset is a rigid transform from the arm's flange frame to the frame the controller
# actually servos, and it is applied INSIDE the kinematic model rather than as a display
# transform. That distinction is the whole point: the Jacobian is then computed to the
# real tip, which is what the RCM constraint needs in order to know the true shaft line.
#
# This exists because tip offsets change constantly during calibration and experiments.
# The v1.4 reference exposed the equivalent only as an OROCOS deployer operation, which
# meant it could not be scripted, logged, or set from a launch file. Here it is a
# service, and every accepted change is published on ~/tool_tip_offset for the recording.
#
# Units are METRES and the transform is flange -> tip, expressed in the flange frame.
# Note the sign convention differs from the v1.4 operation, which took millimetres and
# internally negated them; do not port numbers across without converting.
#
# Applied at the top of the next control cycle via a real-time-safe buffer, so calling
# this never blocks the 500 Hz loop. A request whose translation exceeds
# max_tool_tip_offset (a controller parameter) is rejected rather than clamped, because a
# silently clamped tip offset would corrupt the very calibration it is being used for.
geometry_msgs/Pose offset
---
bool success
string message
# Echoed back so a caller can confirm what the controller actually holds, including the
# normalization applied to the quaternion.
geometry_msgs/Pose applied_offset
